1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,223
Sworn is for Tempo Zones.

2
00:00:02,273 --> 00:00:06,768
Only the operator sees every transaction, so before a withdrawal,

3
00:00:06,818 --> 00:00:09,950
a reviewer cannot verify the private batch.

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,950
Sworn makes that private execution checkable, already on our own Zone.

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,789
Sworn turns an operator-supplied batch into evidence anyone can verify.

6
00:00:19,839 --> 00:00:24,144
Tempo's own Zone code runs inside a zero-knowledge VM,

7
00:00:24,194 --> 00:00:29,950
and only the proof and public batch data cross the privacy boundary.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,607
Tempo Zones ship no native ZK proof today.

9
00:00:33,657 --> 00:00:39,093
We compiled Tempo's own Zone verifier for SP1, with its logic unchanged,

10
00:00:39,143 --> 00:00:45,950
bound it to the portal's batch inputs, and verified a test-fixture proof read-only on Moderato.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,730
Separately, on our own one-operator Zone,

12
00:00:48,780 --> 00:00:56,145
the portal settled three batches only after the proof passed, and our sequencer paid a withdrawal.

13
00:00:56,195 --> 00:00:59,852
Then our own sequencer signed a forged batch.

14
00:00:59,902 --> 00:01:04,950
It was rejected: a real proof cannot authorize a different batch.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,301
First buyer: a Zone business whose reviewer cannot reconstruct the witness.

16
00:01:10,351 --> 00:01:15,166
One batch tests demand; repeats and upgrades become Proof Operations.

17
00:01:15,216 --> 00:01:21,004
The market grows with Zones, batches and upgrades, if Zones are adopted.

18
00:01:21,054 --> 00:01:22,950
Later, beside Tempo's TEE.

19
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,617
I build on Tempo's stack, Reth and Revm, and teach it through Fabrknt Dojo.

20
00:01:29,667 --> 00:01:32,950
Uniswap Foundation sponsor prize at ETHGlobal Tokyo;

21
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:39,617
third in Superteam Japan and NTT DOCOMO R&D's side track at Colosseum's Cypherpunk hackathon.

22
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:42,950
Before crypto, fifteen years of banking systems.

23
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,950
Today: testnet, unaudited, no customers yet.

24
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:49,450
Next, one design partner supplies a batch,

25
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:54,950
and its reviewer decides whether the evidence is worth paying for.

26
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,950
Sworn: verifiable evidence for private execution.
